🔹 Step 1: Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/KalyanM45/AI-Project-Gallery.git
cd AI-Project-Gallery
👉 This downloads the project to your local system
________________________________________
🔹 Step 2: Verify Branch Creation Restriction
git checkout -b test-branch
👉 You may get permission issues when pushing:
git push origin test-branch
❌ Error:
permission denied
👉 This shows:
You cannot create branches directly in original repository (no write access)
________________________________________
🔹 Step 3: Fork Repository
1.	Open repository on GitHub 
2.	Click Fork (top-right) 
3.	A copy is created in your account 
________________________________________
🔹 Step 4: Clone Your Fork
git clone https://github.com/your-username/AI-Project-Gallery.git
cd AI-Project-Gallery
________________________________________
🔹 Step 5: Create Feature Branch
git checkout -b GIT-EXAM
________________________________________
🔹 Step 6: Add / Modify Code
Example:
nano program.py
👉 Sample Code:
print("AI Project Updated")
________________________________________
🔹 Step 7: Add, Commit and Push
git add .
git commit -m "Added new feature"
git push origin GIT-EXAM
________________________________________
🔹 Step 8: Create Pull Request
👉 On GitHub:
1.	Open your forked repo 
2.	Click Compare & pull request 
3.	Base → original repo 
4.	Compare → your GIT-EXAM branch 
5.	Click Create Pull Request 
________________________________________
🔹 Step 9: Resolve Merge Conflicts (If Any)
git pull origin main
If conflict appears:
<<<<<<< HEAD
your code
=======
other code
>>>>>>> branch
👉 Fix manually → then:
git add .
git commit -m "Resolved conflicts"
git push
________________________________________
🔹 Step 10: Update PR After Changes
👉 After pushing:
•	PR updates automatically 
•	Reviewer can approve and merge 
________________________________________
🧠 Viva Points (VERY IMPORTANT ⭐)
•	Clone → copy repo locally 
•	Fork → create personal copy 
•	Branch → isolate feature development 
•	Pull Request → propose changes 
•	Merge Conflict → occurs when same file edited

